    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-f/q2",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q2-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The number of bottles of red wine sold by a local supermarket over a two week period is shown below. 22,  14,  11,  33,  32,  45,  4,  12,  13,  20,  27,  44,  30,  15. a) Display the above data in an ordered stem and leaf diagram. ( ) 3 b) Calculate the mean and the standard deviation of the data. ( ) 4 c) Find the median and the quartiles of the data and use them to determine if there are any outliers. ( ) 5 d) Draw a suitably labelled box plot for this data. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q2-question-2.svg\" alt=\"e) Determine with justification the skewness of the data. ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q2-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The stem represents tens and the leaf represents units. [B1]\" style=\"--madas-width:544.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q2-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Stem Leaves 0 4 1 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 2 0, 2, 7 3 0, 2, 3 4 4, 5 Key 1 | 3 = 13 bottles. [M1] [A1] (b) With P x = 322, P x2 = 9458, [B1] n = 14, the mean is 322/14 = 23 . [A1] The standard deviation is q 9458/14 −232 ≈12.11 [A1] bottles: [A1] (c) The middle two values are 20 and 22. [B1] The middle values of the lower and upper halves are 13 and 32.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q2-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Hence Q1 = 13, [A1] median = 21, [A1] Q3 = 32. [A1] The middle pair average to (20 + 22)/2 = 21. The lower quartile is the fourth observation, the upper the eleventh: Thus Q3 −Q1 = 32 −13 . = 19 The IQR is 19 and the outlier fences are −15.5 and 60.5, from 13 −1.5(19) and 32 + 1.5(19). Both extreme observations, 4 and 45, lie inside, so there are no outliers: [A1] (d) Use minimum 4, maximum 45 and the three quartiles: [M1] [M1] [A1] (e) The mean lies above the median and the upper half has a greater spread: [B1] Numerically Q3 −Q2 = 32 −21 = 11 &gt; 21 −13 . = 8 = Q2 −Q1\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q2-solution-4.svg\" alt=\"The data show positive skew. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:269.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 2 is 17 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The number of bottles of red wine sold by a local supermarket over a two week period is shown below. 22,  14,  11,  33,  32,  45,  4,  12,  13,  20,  27,  44,  30,  15. a) Display the above data in an ordered stem and leaf diagram. ( ) 3 b) Calculate the mean and the standard deviation of the data. ( ) 4 c) Find the median and the quartiles of the data and use them to determine if there are any outliers. ( ) 5 d) Draw a suitably labelled box plot for this data. ( ) 3 e) Determine with justification the skewness of the data. ( ) 2"
