    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-f/q3",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q3-question-1.svg\" alt=\"During the winter months, in a certain village in Scotland, the probability of a day having severe fog is 0.06 . a) Find the probability that in a given week there will be … ( ) 2 i. … no day with severe fog. ( ) 2 ii. … three or more days with severe fog. It is known that on a given week there were three or more days with severe fog. b) Determine the probability that there were exactly three days with severe fog in that week. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let X be the number of foggy days in a week: Model the days as independent with constant probability 0.06, so X ∼B(7, 0.06). (a) (i) P(X = 0) = 0.947 ≈0.6485 . [M1] [A1] (ii) 2 ! 7 0.06k0.947−k ≈0.006294 . P(X ≥3) = 1 − X [M1] [A1] k k=0 (b) The numerator is 7 ! (0.06)3(0.94)4 = 0.00590286 . . . . 3 To obtain the denominator use\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"1 −P(X ≤2) = 0.006294 . . . . Exactly three days is a subset of at least three days: [M1] Hence 7 (0.06)3(0.94)4 3 P(X = 3 | X ≥3) = ≈0.9378 . [M1] [A1] P(X ≥3)\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 3 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "During the winter months, in a certain village in Scotland, the probability of a day having severe fog is 0.06 . a) Find the probability that in a given week there will be … ( ) 2 i. … no day with severe fog. ( ) 2 ii. … three or more days with severe fog. It is known that on a given week there were three or more days with severe fog. b) Determine the probability that there were exactly three days with severe fog in that week. ( ) 3"
