    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-f/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The continuous random variable X is Normally distributed with a mean of 9.5 and a standard deviation of 1.3. a) Find ( P X &gt; 12 ) . ( ) 4 ( ) 4 b) Determine the value of a such that ( P X &lt; a ) = 0.1587\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Subtract 9.5 and divide by 1.3, so the cutoff becomes 2.5/1.3 = 1.92308 . . . . The area to its left is 0.97276 . . .. Hence P(X &gt; 12) = 1 −Φ((12 −9.5)/1.3) ≈0.02724 . [M1] Use the normal model [M1] standardise 12 [M1] take the upper tail [A1] evaluate\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) (a −9.5)/1.3 = Φ−1(0.1587) ≈−0.99982. [B1] [A1] The upper-tail area is 1 −0.1587 = 0.8413. The left-tail quantile is approximately −1, giving a −9.5 ≈−1.3. Hence a ≈8.20 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The continuous random variable X is Normally distributed with a mean of 9.5 and a standard deviation of 1.3. a) Find ( P X > 12 ) . ( ) 4 ( ) 4 b) Determine the value of a such that ( P X < a ) = 0.1587"
  },
