    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-f/q7",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The events A and B satisfy P ( ) A = 0.6 , ( ) P B = 0.52 and  ( P A ∪ B ) = 0.88 . a) Find the value of ( P A ∩ B ) and hence illustrate this probability information in a fully completed Venn diagram. ( ) 4 b) Determine … i. … ( P B A . ) ( ) 2 ii. … ( P A B ′ ′ . ) ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q7-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) State, giving a reason, whether A and B are … i. … statistically independent. ( ) 2 ii. … mutually exclusive. ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:584.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) By inclusion and exclusion, P(A ∩B) = 0.60 + 0.52 −0.88 . [M1] [A1] = 0.24 The A-only region is 0.60 −0.24 = 0.36, the B-only region 0.52 −0.24 = 0.28, and neither 1 −0.88 = 0.12. [M1] [A1] (b) (i) P(B | A) = 0.24/0.60 . [M1] [A1] = 0.40\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(ii) P(A′ | B′) = 0.12/(1 −0.52) . [M1] [A1] = 0.25 (c) (i) The intersection is 0.24 while the product is 0.60(0.52) = 0.312, [B1] so the events are dependent: The source also checks P(B | A) = 0.40̸ = 0.52 = P(B) . [A1] (ii) The intersection has positive probability, so the events can occur together: [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 12 marks.</p>"
