    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-f/q8",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A car of mass 1500 kg is towing a trailer of mass 1000 kg by means of a light inextensible rope. The car is experiencing a constant air resistance of 200 N , while the corresponding constant air resistance on the trailer is 300 N . The car and trailer are modelled as particles, with the tow rope remaining taut and horizontal throughout the motion. a) Given that the driving force acting on the car is 750 N , determine … i. … the acceleration of the system. ( ) 3 ii. … the tension in the tow rope. ( ) 2 Later in the journey, the car and the trailer are ascending on a road which inclined at 5° to the horizontal. The air resistance on the car and trailer are unchanged.\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q8-question-2.svg\" alt=\"b) Assuming that the system now moves with constant speed, calculate … i. … a new figure for the tension in the tow rope. ( ) 3 ii. … a new figure for the driving force of the car. ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Worked solution diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:528.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) Resolve forwards, with common acceleration a and tension T. For the car, 750 −T −200 = 1500a. For the trailer, T −300 = 1000a. (i) Adding gives 250 = 2500a, [B1] so a = 0.10 m s−2 . [M1] [A1] (ii) The trailer equation gives T −300 = 1000(0.10) = 100, so adding 300 gives T = 400 N . [M1] [A1] (b) On the ascent, take the rope parallel to the road: The acceleration is zero. (i) For the trailer, T = 300 + 1000g sin 5◦≈1154 N . [M1] [M1] [A1] (ii) For the car D −T −200 −1500g sin 5◦= 0.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q8-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Substitute T = 300 + 1000g sin 5◦to obtain D = 500 + (1500 + 1000)g sin 5◦. The driving force balances both resistances and the entire weight component along the slope, giving 500 + 2500g sin 5◦≈2635 N . [M1] [A1] Source note. The printed phrase about a horizontal rope conflicts with the drawing used in the handwritten ascent solution. Part (b) follows that solution’s geometry.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 8 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A car of mass 1500 kg is towing a trailer of mass 1000 kg by means of a light inextensible rope. The car is experiencing a constant air resistance of 200 N , while the corresponding constant air resistance on the trailer is 300 N . The car and trailer are modelled as particles, with the tow rope remaining taut and horizontal throughout the motion. a) Given that the driving force acting on the car is 750 N , determine … i. … the acceleration of the system. ( ) 3 ii. … the tension in the tow rope. ( ) 2 Later in the journey, the car and the trailer are ascending on a road which inclined at 5° to the horizontal. The air resistance on the car and trailer are unchanged. b) Assuming that the system now moves with constant speed, calculate … i. … a new figure for the tension in the tow rope. ( ) 3 ii. … a new figure for the driving force of the car. ( ) 2"
