  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-f/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A particle is projected from a point O on level horizontal ground with speed of ms− at an angle θ to the horizontal, where 1 3 21 tan θ = . 4 The particle is moving freely under gravity and lands at a point A on the ground, which is 43.2 m away from O . a) Find the time it takes the particle to travel from O to A . ( ) 3 b) Determine the greatest height above the ground reached by the particle during its flight. ( ) 2 c) Show that the particle remains at a height of at least 4.5 m above ground for exactly 5 17 seconds. ( ) 5\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-f/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
